      "next_deadline": "Follows HCD's state CDBG and HOME NOFA calendar; the County held its 2026 CDBG public meeting on March 18, 2026 and hearing on March 24, 2026. A developer wanting the County as applicant or co-applicant for a state rental program should approach the County Administrator's Office before the HCD NOFA opens.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Yolo County has no county gap loan program for rental housing and no development NOFA. Its state CDBG and HOME capacity is small and committed to homeowner rehab and homebuyer programs, and the County issued an RFP in September 2026 for housing program consulting (loan management, grant writing) to run these programs. The practical County role for a developer is the resolution or co-applicant for state programs (HOME rental, Joe Serna farmworker housing, MHP) in the unincorporated communities (Esparto, Madison, Knights Landing, Dunnigan, Clarksburg). The Board created a Farmworker Housing Ad Hoc Subcommittee in May 2025 and the March 2026 Board calendar listed hearings on a farmworker housing planning grant application. The three cities (Davis, Woodland, West Sacramento) run their own programs and are Pass 3. State funds trigger prevailing wage and federal cross-cutting rules.",
